{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.62,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["J5", "U1", "U6"],
      "pins": ["J5.1", "J5.2", "U1.13", "U6.1", "U6.2"],
      "nets": ["/Microcontroller/HEATER", "GND"],
      "observed": "A user-accessible screw terminal J5 is connected directly between the ESP32 GPIO1 / heater-control net and GND: J5 pin 2 is on /Microcontroller/HEATER and J5 pin 1 is on GND. That same net also drives U6 IN and DIAG_EN and U1 GPIO1.",
      "expected": "The specification describes a single heater output path driven from ESP32 GPIO1 into the smart high-side switch, with the heater load connector J6 on U6 OUT. It does not describe a screw terminal tied directly to the GPIO1 control net, and standard practice would not expose a firmware-driven logic output to a user-connectable terminal shorted to ground without firmware handling or protection.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "net (code \"4\") (name \"/Microcontroller/HEATER\") ... (node (ref \"J5\") (pin \"2\") ... ) (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"13\") ... ) (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"1\") ... ) (node (ref \"U6\") (pin \"2\") ... )"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "net (code \"13\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"J5\") (pin \"1\") ... )"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Drives a single **heater output** net through a smart high-side switch (`U6`, TPS1H200AQDGNRQ1) switched from the ESP32's GPIO1"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "`OUT` (pin 7) feeds the heater connector `J6` pin 2"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If J5 is shorted or wired by a user, GPIO1 is forced low and the heater switch is disabled regardless of firmware state; if a voltage is applied to J5, the ESP32 GPIO1 and heater-control path can be damaged. This adds an undocumented external override path on a critical heater-control signal.",
      "confidence": 0.62
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The main deviation is the undocumented screw terminal J5 tied directly across the GPIO1 heater-control net and GND; the rest of the power, thermocouple, SPI, heater-switch, and USB circuitry matches the specification."
}

